    "updated_at": "2022-08-02T23:43:15Z",
    "body": "But this particular test is against [HTMLOrSVGImageElement](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#htmlorsvgimageelement)'s third step:\r\n\r\n> If image has an [intrinsic width](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-images/#intrinsic-width) or [intrinsic height](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-images/#intrinsic-height) (or both) equal to zero, then return bad.\r\n\r\nPassing a zero width HTMLCanvasElement does throw as specced in every UA. Firefox and Chrome also do throw on broken images (though they seem to disagree on what makes a broken image...)\r\n\r\nA few quick tests: https://jsfiddle.net/6wn1rof3/\r\n\r\nI'm not sure why the specs need to be changed here? But maybe I'm missing something.",
